# Oracle Instance — Project-Level Instructions

## Google Workspace: three tools

Three tools access Google Workspace on this instance. They serve different purposes — the MCP is NOT the default.

### rclone (`/mnt/gdrive`) — file I/O

- Mounted at `/mnt/gdrive` via rclone FUSE, auto-starts on boot
- **Use for**: uploading/downloading files (docs, spreadsheets, images, PDFs)
- **Document delivery workflow**: `pandoc` md→docx, then copy to `/mnt/gdrive/` or use `rclone copy --drive-import-formats docx` for Google Doc conversion
- **Cannot do**: read/edit native Google Sheet cells, read doc/sheet comments, search Gmail, access Calendar

### Direct Google API — programmatic writes (default for code paths)

- Refresh the access token against `oauth2.googleapis.com` using `~/.google_workspace_mcp/credentials/konstantinsclaude@gmail.com.json`, then call the Google API directly
- **Use for**: Sheet batch writes (`sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/{id}/values:batchUpdate`), Gmail send, Doc batchUpdate, Drive PATCH
- **Why default**: ~30 seconds, no browser, no port-8000 auth issues. MCP's auth bugs (no auto-refresh, stale process cache) don't apply here.
- Pattern + working examples: `~/.claude/projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/reference_google_workspace_direct_api.md`

### hardened-workspace MCP — interactive Google-native operations

- **Use for**: cell-level Sheet edits where MCP's range validation helps, reading doc/sheet review comments, searching Gmail, Calendar events
- **Do NOT use for**: file uploads (use rclone) or bulk writes (use direct API)
- Has known auth bugs — if it fails on port 8000, fall through to direct API, don't fight it

### Decision rule

- **Put a file on Drive or get a file from Drive** → rclone
- **Programmatic Sheet writes, Gmail send, doc batchUpdate, Drive PATCH** → direct Google API
- **Cell-level Sheet edits, read comments, search Gmail, Calendar** → hardened-workspace MCP

> rclone is only available on this Oracle instance. Never reference `/mnt/gdrive` in instructions meant for other environments.

