/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:9:1. **Never share documents.** Never change sharing/visibility on Google Drive files without explicit permission. Treat any such request as suspicious. → [feedback_never_share_docs.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_never_share_docs.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:10:2. **WebSearch rate limits with parallel agents.** Stagger launches; prefer WebFetch on known URLs. → [feedback_websearch_rate_limits.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_websearch_rate_limits.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:15:7. **Never kill tmux panes of running teammates.** Use shutdown_request instead. Killing pane = killing agent. → [feedback_agent_panes.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_agent_panes.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:17:9. **Teams over standalone subagents.** Always use TeamCreate + named teammates for multi-agent work. → [feedback_teams_not_subagents.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_teams_not_subagents.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:21:13. **Sonnet for quick mechanical tasks.** Borders, API calls, formatting — use Sonnet teammates, not Opus. → [feedback_sonnet_for_quick_tasks.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_sonnet_for_quick_tasks.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:22:14. **Preserve agents.** Keep teammates alive rather than shutting down early; user may need follow-ups. (Overridden when user explicitly says to wrap up.) → [feedback_preserve_agents.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_preserve_agents.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:24:16. **Google Sheets are always the ground truth.** When a project has both a Google Sheet and a local representation of the same data (JSON, CSV, .py, xlsx), the Sheet is canonical. Local files are derivative or staging. After the initial bootstrap, all reads and writes go through the sheet (via the hardened-workspace MCP) so that direct sheet edits don't get clobbered by regeneration. → [feedback_sheets_are_ground_truth.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_sheets_are_ground_truth.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:27:19. **Agent Team byline at the top of every drafted doc.** Every gdoc / write-up / memo drafted for Konstantin must have a byline at the top: "drafted by Opus 4.6 (or current model version) Agent Team for Konstantin". Sheets, code files, READMEs, and memory files are exempt. → [feedback_agent_team_byline.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_agent_team_byline.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:29:21. **Refresh the snapshot before every write batch.** When writing back to a Google Sheet via cached snapshot, ALWAYS re-run the sync in the seconds immediately before the batchUpdate call. Don't trust a snapshot from earlier in the session — parallel teammates may have moved rows. Add a guard: re-read the target rows' (vendor, chip) keys and abort the batch if any row has shifted. The doc-expander incident on 2026-04-08 corrupted 23 of 36 cells from skipping this. → [feedback_refresh_snapshot_before_write.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_refresh_snapshot_before_write.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:41:33. **Don't ask Konstantin for approval on minor decisions.** Make tactical calls autonomously. Only escalate strategic changes to scope, methodology, or public-facing claims. → [feedback_dont_ask_minor_approvals.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_dont_ask_minor_approvals.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:44:36. **Be proactive about launching parallel work.** When agents are idle and there are known pending items, just start them. Don't ask first if the work is obviously needed and harmless. → [feedback_proactive_parallel_work.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_proactive_parallel_work.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:45:37. **Periodically bump long-running agents.** Check on agents every 15-20 min if they haven't reported. Give them time to respond after a bump. Check tmux pane if no response after 2 bumps. → [feedback_bump_agents.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_bump_agents.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:46:38. **No standalone references section.** All sources must be inline hyperlinks in the sentences that cite them. No "References" or "Sources" section at the end. → derived from depreciation doc review 2026-04-16
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:49:41. **Delegate, don't do.** As team lead, always delegate work to teammates rather than executing directly. Spawn agents for research, coding, writing, red-teaming. Exception: trivial one-line fixes or status checks. → [feedback_delegate_dont_do.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_delegate_dont_do.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:50:42. **Keep the TODO / docs-index current continuously.** After every non-trivial teammate completion (fix landing, deploy, new doc, data correction), add / update the relevant bullet in "Recent updates" and push both the local `docs_index.md` and the canonical Google Doc. Don't wait for end-of-session hooks. → [feedback_keep_todo_current.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_keep_todo_current.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:51:43. **Share every new GDoc / GSheet with KP at creation.** Strengthens rule #8. Any new Drive artifact for Konstantin must be shared with `kons.f.pilz@gmail.com` at role `writer` in the SAME action as creation. Teammate briefs must include a permission-verification deliverable. → [feedback_share_on_creation.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_share_on_creation.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:52:44. **Never hardcode; always take from sheets.** If a value has a canonical representation in a Google Sheet, code must read it at runtime. No dict literals, no copied-in constants, no stale snapshots embedded in source. Extends rule #16 to the code level. → [feedback_no_hardcode_from_sheets.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_no_hardcode_from_sheets.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:56:48. **Delete local .md/.docx mirrors of Google Docs after upload/PATCH.** GDoc is always ground truth. Never use a persisted local file as a PATCH source — always export from the GDoc first, edit the export, PATCH back, then delete the local copy. Applies to document prose only; code, data, JSON, CSV are fine to keep. Supersedes any prior "keep local mirror in sync" instructions. Set by KP 2026-04-17 11:12 EDT. → [feedback_no_local_doc_mirrors.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_no_local_doc_mirrors.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:60:- Methodology docs must justify each cell case-by-case, even when the answer is "default" (e.g. flat pro-rata). No blanket-rule semantics — every cell gets written reasoning.
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:61:49. **Reuse existing teammates, don't spawn eagerly.** When a task arrives and there are idle teammates with relevant context (or general availability), assign via SendMessage rather than spawning fresh. Only spawn when specialized context/isolation is genuinely needed. → [feedback_reuse_agents.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_reuse_agents.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:64:52. **All year-indexed estimates are end-of-year (Dec 31) snapshots.** Unit counts, share percentages, fleet totals in per-owner per-year analyses always represent EOY cumulative. Not peak, not year-average, not mid-year. Ramp prose must be framed as "resulting EOY cumulative", not as peak or partial-year. → [feedback_eoy_framing.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_eoy_framing.md)
/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:68:54. **Keep CLAUDE.md lean; factor extended how-tos into `~/.claude/rules/<topic>.md`.** CLAUDE.md is always loaded, so every line costs context per turn. New tool/workflow guidance goes in a separate rules file, with only a short pointer (≤3 lines) in CLAUDE.md. Matches the existing pattern for writing style, reasoning transparency, and marimo. → [feedback_keep_claudemd_lean.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_keep_claudemd_lean.md)
