/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:87:Wed May 20 2026 — Memory and writing-rule scaffolding cleanup. Five empirical-research confidence memos merged into [feedback_confidence_in_empirical_work.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_confidence_in_empirical_work.md). Six citation memos merged into [feedback_citations_in_empirical_work.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_citations_in_empirical_work.md). New meta-rule [feedback_teammate_genre_context.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_teammate_genre_context.md): when spawning teammates for non-empirical work (persuasive memos, op-eds, candidate memos), give them genre context, don't auto-propagate the empirical feedback set. Empirical-only memos got a Context line at the top of the body. writing-style.md got a pre-flight genre question and a promoted read-aloud rule at the top. Triggered by an incident where another Claude instance applied empirical chip-pipeline rules to a persuasive research-agenda memo.
