/home/ubuntu/.claude/feedback_log.md:149:73. **Parallelize disjoint Sheet edits.** Multiple agents editing explicit non-overlapping cells/ranges should write concurrently; do not put the whole workbook or full agent turns behind one lock. Serialize only overlaps, structural/broad-formatting changes, and final reconciliation. Re-read stable labels, use narrow writes, and run one workbook-wide QA afterward. This session was slow because safe regional edits were unnecessarily queued; the actual failures were nested locking, command syntax, and a structural circular reference—not concurrent different-cell edits. → [feedback_parallel_sheet_edits.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_parallel_sheet_edits.md) (KP 2026-08-13)
